            'Present: Played as a loud, social party variant for large groups that keeps the memory and book-collecting core of Go Fish.',
          ],
          evolution: 'Backstab Fish takes the basic Go Fish structure and extends it to a 108-card pack, with players tracking up to eight copies of each rank and using quantity asks to swing large numbers of cards at once.',
          cultural: 'Around Adelaide tables it is treated as a vocal, social deduction variant where calling specific opponents and quantities is part strategy and part performance.',
