          deckDescription: 'Two standard 52-card decks combined plus four Jokers (108 cards total). Four suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs), thirteen ranks each per deck; four Jokers act as wild cards. Used for Backstab Fish and other quartet or set-collection games with two decks.',
          suitDescription: 'Four French suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs) in duplicate. Matching or capturing is by rank or combination as the rules specify; suits may matter for building or capturing in this game.',
          rankDescription: 'Thirteen ranks per suit in each deck (ace through two). Pairs or sets of the same rank may capture; when two decks are used, multiple cards of the same rank appear. Game rules define capture and scoring.',
